      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened May 12, 1891, and was renamed Creede on July 1, 1891, after Nicholas C.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creede%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Creede Historical Museum, housed in the old Denver and Rio Grande Western Railroad depot, displays artifacts from the town’s mining past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://colorado.wiki/a/Creede,_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Creede Repertory Theatre, founded in 1966, remains the region’s most prominent cultural institution, performing in a historic 1930s movie house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://colorado.wiki/a/Creede,_Colorado",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
